# migration-compat.baseline — grandfathered rule-9 violations.
#
# One `<file>:<class>` per line; see scripts/ci/lint-migration-compat.sh
# for the class list. Every entry is a migration that already shipped
# before the rule-9 gate existed (audit-2026-07-23, CID-14) and that the
# lint cannot mechanically prove is old-binary-safe.
#
# Most entries are `add-constraint`: an `ALTER TABLE … ADD CONSTRAINT
# … CHECK (col IN (…))` that WIDENS an existing enum-ish check (the
# cctp / blend / mev / phoenix event-kind sets) or a primary-key
# granularity change. Widening is safe; the lint cannot tell widening
# from narrowing, so these were grandfathered rather than re-litigated.
# `0113:drop-table` and `0115:drop-view` are genuine destructive
# migrations that shipped under the old, unenforced policy.
#
# SHRINK-ONLY (CS-098): a stale entry fails the lint, and
# scripts/ci/lint-baseline-growth.sh requires an explicit
# `Baseline-Growth:` commit trailer for any addition. NEW migrations
# should use the inline `-- migration-compat:ok <reason>` marker
# instead of growing this file.
